# TSK 4.12.1 and its image-format modules keep process-global allocations alive
# after the handle is closed. LeakSanitizer reports them because those C
# libraries are neither instrumented nor responsible for freeing that state, so
# the reports say nothing about OpenForensic Imager's own allocations.
#
# Leaks allocated by instrumented Rust code still fail the run.
leak:libtsk
leak:libvmdk
leak:libvhdi
leak:libewf
leak:libcdata
